12:
13:    Input structure:
14:    - The background is the most common color.
15:    - The scene contains several separated monochrome foreground objects.
16:    - Exactly one 4-connected monochrome foreground object has the largest pixel area.
17:
18:    Rule:
19:    - Find all 4-connected monochrome foreground components.
20:    - Select the unique largest component by area.
21:    - Output that component in its own bounding box, with background in all non-object cells.
22:
23:    Key insight:
24:    - The desired crop is identified by connected foreground area, while the smaller objects are distractors.
25:    """
